{
  "slug": "workshop-mode",
  "name": "Workshop Mode",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Voice-triggered dev environment setup for macOS. Type a phrase in Claude Code and your terminals snap into a grid across your screens, music starts playing, and apps tile into place. Configurable trigger phrase, music, terminal themes, and multi-monitor layouts.\n\nAla Tony Stark.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **2 skills** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (2): `workshop` (Activate Workshop Mode to arrange your dev environment, or preview the layout with --dry-run), `workshop-setup` (Interactively configure Workshop Mode — music, triggers, terminal count, app layout, and more)\n- **Hooks** (1): `UserPromptSubmit`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install workshop-mode@claude-community` from `kayossouza/claude-workshop`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 2,
    "hook": 1
  },
